<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
    NorthstarIQ - Revenue Operations Intelligence Platform
    Deployment manifest

    STATUS: Phase 0A - intentionally EMPTY.

    No Salesforce business metadata has been designed, created, or deployed.
    This manifest is populated in Phase 1 (Salesforce Foundation & Security)
    and grows as each capability is implemented.

    The Salesforce CLI default template ships this file pre-populated with
    wildcard <members>*</members> entries for ApexClass, ApexComponent, ApexPage,
    ApexTestSuite, ApexTrigger, AuraDefinitionBundle, LightningComponentBundle and
    StaticResource. Those have been removed deliberately:

      - This is a declarative, Flow-first architecture. Apex requires justification
        recorded in an ADR (see CLAUDE.md 16). Listing Apex types by default would
        misrepresent the intended design.
      - No Aura or Lightning Web Components are planned.
      - Wildcard manifests retrieve whatever happens to exist in the org, which
        conflicts with treating source control - not the org - as the source of truth.

    Expected metadata types once implementation begins (Phase 1+):

        CustomObject          custom fields, validation rules, record types
        Flow                  record-triggered and screen automation
        CustomMetadata        metadata-driven business rules (routing, segmentation,
                              scoring weights, SLA configuration)
        PermissionSet         least-privilege access model
        PermissionSetGroup    persona-level access composition
        SharingRules          record visibility beyond OWD
        Role                  role hierarchy
        Group                 public groups
        Queue                 routing and exception queues
        DuplicateRule         duplicate management
        MatchingRule          identity matching
        Report / Dashboard    operational reporting
        GlobalValueSet        governed picklist taxonomies

    Add entries explicitly and deliberately. Do not reintroduce wildcards.
-->
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
